  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2510.16258v1</id>
    <title>Embody 3D: A Large-scale Multimodal Motion and Behavior Dataset</title>
    <updated>2025-10-17T23:06:36Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.16258v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.16258v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>The Codec Avatars Lab at Meta introduces Embody 3D, a multimodal dataset of 500 individual hours of 3D motion data from 439 participants collected in a multi-camera collection stage, amounting to over 54 million frames of tracked 3D motion. The dataset features a wide range of single-person motion data, including prompted motions, hand gestures, and locomotion; as well as multi-person behavioral and conversational data like discussions, conversations in different emotional states, collaborative activities, and co-living scenarios in an apartment-like space. We provide tracked human motion including hand tracking and body shape, text annotations, and a separate audio track for each participant.</summary>
    <category term="cs.CV" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2025-10-17T23:06:36Z</published>
